- the 0136 reservation.
I02. Prime's conditions, which override my 05.11 §2 closure rule:
- **SP-01.** Review text does not close a batch. Held and correction-required stay open and blocked. Completion needs a candidate-bound, explicit terminal declaration.
- **SP-02.** The facets stay independent. Publication is not completion. A summary never hides an unreleased, held or ambiguous item. No live observation is projected backward onto a commit.
- **SP-03.** The output is not a v1 record. It is a separately tagged projection over declared scope only.
- **SP-04.** The primary is matched on origin book, page and batch. More than one matching complete candidate is ambiguous unless an explicit selection resolves it. A bound review must match the specific member and receipt. Labels are not grants.
I03. DEC-3 is exercised in fixtures as typed bindings only. DEC-4 is already visible in this page's own header ("Release and claim: recorded in the Return pointer"). DEC-1, DEC-2 and DEC-5 are not needed and are not used.

## Choices (routine, made before code)
C01. Lab: `labs/state-projection-pass01/` with state_projection.py, README.md, tests/test_state_projection.py and demo.py. Standard library only. CLI:
`project --input OBS.json [--inspect] [--json]`.
- The input is one strict JSON document, `state-observations/1`: a fixture scope, plus a list of typed batch observations.
- The output is `state-projection/1`, written to stdout.
- The tool writes nothing.
C02. Observations are supplied declarations, and each carries a `provenance` of `supplied-commit` (with a commit) or `supplied-live`. The tool never claims to have read Git. Member custody comes only from the pinned inspector, as a separate, timestamped, live block, and only when `--inspect` is given. A live result never sets a commit-time facet.
C03. Closure: a batch is `completed` only when all of these hold:
- the release is recorded;
- the primary candidate is resolved and complete, as observed live, or supplied as `supplied-commit` custody evidence;
- a bound review names that member and receipt;
- the review carries `terminal: "completed"`, an explicit terminal declaration, and its binding matches.
Anything else is not complete:
- held, or correction-required, is open and blocked;
- text-only review is `review-present, unresolved`;
- a stale binding is `re-review-required`.
C04. The lane view lists every open item, in declared order. It never picks one, and never uses the newest or highest number.
C05. Strict input: exact keys, typed values, duplicate-key and duplicate-id refusal, and unknown versions refused before any iteration. Exit codes: 0 projected with no attention; 1 projected with attention; 2 refused, nothing projected.
C06. The inspector is pin-checked, together with its helper, before every launch, with the argument-array form `[sys.executable, "-I", "-B", path, "inspect", …]`. The projection reuses the inspector's reported origin, status and receipt. It does not re-validate custody.
C07. Tests use real reserve, capture and inspect on disposable books for every custody case. Text-only cases need no member. W1-W7 come in as scenario input with corrected expectations, recorded additively in the contract.

